<div class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between">
  <div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy-900">System Health</h1>
    <p class="mt-0.5 text-sm text-gray-500">
      Platform-wide operational diagnostics — visible to platform administrators only.
    </p>
  </div>
  <%= link "Dashboard", to: ~p"/admin/dashboard", class: "text-sm font-medium text-gray-400 hover:text-navy-600" %>
</div>

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
  <div class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="section-title mb-3">Scheduler Heartbeats</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
      <%= for scheduler <- @schedulers do %>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="font-medium text-navy-900"><%= format_scheduler_name(scheduler.name) %></div>
            <div class="text-xs text-gray-400"><%= format_last_tick(scheduler.last_tick) %></div>
          </div>
          <span class={status_badge_class(scheduler.stale?)}>
            <%= if scheduler.stale?, do: "Stale", else: "OK" %>
          </span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="section-title mb-3">Malware Scanner</h2>
    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">Failures (last hour)</span>
        <span class={status_badge_class(@scanner_failure_count > 0)}>
          <%= @scanner_failure_count %>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs text-gray-400"><%= format_last_failure(@scanner_last_failure_at) %></div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
        A rising count is the earliest signal of a broken ClamAV install — see the deployment runbook §8.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card p-5">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3">
      <h2 class="section-title">Database Pool</h2>
      <span class={status_badge_class(not @pool_healthy?)}>
        <%= if @pool_healthy?, do: "OK", else: "Warning" %>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">Samples observed</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-navy-900"><%= @pool_stats.sample_count %></span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">Last queue time</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-navy-900"><%= @pool_stats.last_queue_time_ms || "—" %> ms</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">Max queue time (current window)</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-navy-900"><%= @pool_stats.max_queue_time_ms || "—" %> ms</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
        Warns at <%= @pool_stats.warning_threshold_ms %> ms. The max resets every 5 minutes (window started <%= format_timestamp(@pool_stats.max_queue_time_window_started_at) %>) so a resolved spike doesn't sit here looking like an ongoing problem.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="section-title mb-3">Disk Space</h2>
    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">KYC upload directory</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-navy-900"><%= format_bytes(@kyc_disk) %></span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
        The Postgres host's own disk space is a separate machine in most real deployments and isn't observable from
        this app — monitor it directly at the host level.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card p-5">
    <h2 class="section-title mb-3">Backups</h2>
    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">Latest</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-navy-900"><%= format_backup_summary(@latest_backup) %></span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <span class="text-gray-500">Failures (last 24h)</span>
        <span class={status_badge_class(@backup_failure_count > 0)}>
          <%= @backup_failure_count %>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="text-xs text-gray-400"><%= format_last_failure(@backup_last_failure_at) %></div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
        Scheduler heartbeat above covers "did it run recently" — this covers "did it actually succeed." See the
        deployment runbook §10.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
